# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A raw delimiter carries a scope themes colour"

# Across the shipped grammars a verbatim delimiter takes its colour either from a region
# scoped comment.* or string.*, or from a scope of its own — shell gives a heredoc marker
# keyword.operator.heredoc, Perl gives POD constant.language. This grammar scopes its raw
# regions meta.*, which no theme colours, so the delimiters carry their own scope. It reads
# keyword.control rather than keyword.operator: six of the fifteen shipped themes set
# keyword.operator to the default foreground, and every one of them colours keyword.control.

```js
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.codeblock.tiddlywiki5 keyword.control.raw.fence.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.raw.markup.begin.tiddlywiki5
var a = 1;
```

A paragraph carrying `inline code` and ``a double tick``.
#                    ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 keyword.control.raw.tick.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.raw.markup.single.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                                      ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 keyword.control.raw.tick.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.raw.markup.double.begin.tiddlywiki5

$$$text/plain
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.typedblock.tiddlywiki5 keyword.control.raw.typedblock.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.typedblock.begin.tiddlywiki5
a typed block
$$$
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.typedblock.tiddlywiki5 keyword.control.raw.typedblock.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.typedblock.end.tiddlywiki5
